    "title": "Contract details for New York Jets QB Justin Fields",
    "text": "Contracts for the deal agreed between the New York Jets and quarterback Justin Fields have been revealed.On the opening day of the 2025 NFL free agency frenzy on Monday, the Jets signed their presumed next starter under center. Upon first being reported, it was said that the 25-year-old inked a two-year deal in New York.AdvertisementBut NFL contracts seldomly are that simple.With the green and white, Fields inked a contract worth $40 million over the course of those two seasons. Of that, $30M is guaranteed.According to various reports, more details have surfaced.The Jets and general manager Darren Mougey have backloaded Fields' contract a bit.ESPN reports that Fields will have base salaries of $5M and $20M in his deal, respectively. The other $15M comes via a signing bonus.The real interest comes via the salary cap hits. Those are spread out over the next two years at figures of $5M and $23M.Why that's so interesting is because the Jets will also have a $35M dead-cap hit from former quarterback Aaron Rodgers next year. If New York wanted to cut Fields after 2025, a dead hit from him would be $22M, and combined with Rodgers, that would total $57M in dead-cap hits on QBs.AdvertisementBut the Jets still have a couple other million worth hitting their salary cap until at least 2030, regardless. The Athletic reports that Fields' contract has \"void years\" attached to it, which essentially spreads out the cap hits. Reportedly the cap hit in 2027--when Fields' deal is already expired, would be $9M.This article originally appeared on Jets Wire: Contract details for New York Jets QB Justin Fields",
